caption: Gift Traits
tradition-component: gift-traits

A permanent trait purchased directly from a Latent Gift through Spawn is a Gift Trait. If the purchased trait is a stable bodily realization of the Gift's stated capability, that Gift becomes Realized under the Eldritch Core rules. If fewer than ten Gifts have been revealed, the Core then reveals the next Latent Gift; after all ten have been revealed, no replacement is created. The Gift Trait remains a valid Spawn Power Stunt source after the source Gift becomes Realized.

A Gift that was already Realized before Spawn, or is later Realized through another Eldritch Gifts Tradition, may also supply a Spawn Gift Trait if the character possesses an existing permanent ability that is a stable bodily realization of that Gift and satisfies Embodied Gift Scope. Choose one such existing ability as that Gift's Spawn Gift Trait. This does not repurchase or reprice the ability, does not make the Gift Latent again, and does not retroactively subject the original purchase to Spawn Trait Cap; any Spawn Trait later derived from it must obey the normal Spawn rules and Spawn Trait Cap.

A Gift Trait may be used as the source for a Spawn Power Stunt. If that stunt successfully manifests another legal embodied trait, Spawn permits that new trait to be purchased permanently as a Spawn Trait, subject to the normal point cost and Spawn Trait Cap.
